cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the thesis below."
title: "OptNet-Based Constrained Imitation Learning for Cart-Pole Control"
type: thesis
authors:
  - family-names: Jin
    given-names: Enze
year: 2026
institution:
  name: School of Advanced Technology
url: "https://github.com/Kingzner/optnet-cartpole"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Kingzner/optnet-cartpole"
abstract: >-
  A cart-pole controller that learns from expert trajectory-optimisation demonstrations and
  produces its control output through a differentiable quadratic programming layer (OptNet),
  so that the control-force and cart-position limits are part of the model structure rather
  than learned only from data. The OptNet-QP controller is compared against an MLP baseline on
  prediction accuracy, closed-loop rollout behaviour and constraint violation counts.
keywords:
  - optnet
  - differentiable optimization
  - quadratic programming
  - model predictive control
  - imitation learning
  - cart-pole
